    "methylation_promoter_mapping_rule": "A CpG probe is eligible for the promoter-level analysis of frozen gene G if: 1. its IlmnID exists in the selected HM450 SeSAMe beta files; 2. the Illumina v1.2 UCSC_RefGene_Name annotation contains G; 3. the transcript-aligned corresponding UCSC_RefGene_Group entry for G is one of: TSS200, TSS1500, 5'UTR, 1stExon. Where semicolon-separated gene names and gene-group fields contain multiple transcripts, preserve positional alignment between the two fields. A probe satisfying the rule through any transcript of G is eligible once. No cross-reactive/SNP filtering is to be added unless an explicit, authoritative prespecified mask is separately frozen BEFORE outcomes.",
